auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: https://roll6.site
  email: rodrigo@emagine.com.br
  password: {{password}}
}

docs {
  # Roll6 API
  
  Requests inherit Bearer auth from the collection; `User/Login` stores `token` and `User/Login player` stores
  `playerToken` (requests made as the player use it explicitly). Create requests store ids as runtime variables used
  by the following requests.
  
  Running the whole collection in order (Runner) works end to end and can be repeated:
  - `User/Register` creates the main user from the environment (`email`, `password`); later runs get 409, which is fine.
  - `User/Change password back` restores the password; `User/Register player` creates a new player each run.
  - Each folder creates an extra record just to exercise its DELETE, so the records used by later folders survive.
  
  Folders: User, ApiKey (019), Image/Document uploads, Token, MapModel, Campaign, Map, Character, CampaignCharacter,
  MapToken, Npc/CampaignNpc/MapNpc (013), Turn (016), CampaignPlan (018), Transfer (021).
  
  Uploads (`Image/*`) need S3 (DigitalOcean Spaces) credentials on the API; everything that uses `imageFileName`,
  `sheetFileName` depends on them.
  
  Credentials live in the environments; in Production they are secret variables (set them in Bruno, they are not
  saved in the file).
}
